  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLIMALAB- Sustainable approach to environmental degradation in Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">We will achieve the programme goals through two key objectives:
Objective One: Build climate-resilient communities and provide clean energy
Christian Aid and our partners will directly work with marginalised families, to promote a transfer to clean energy&#xa0;&#xa0;with the introduction of community appropriate technologies&#xa0;such as biodigesters and eco-efficient stoves. This work will run alongside agroforestry activities related to climate change adaptation, like diversifying crops and introducing small livestock such as goats and sheep.&#xa0;By promoting diverse crops, we will be providing food security in the short-term, and in the long-term, more ambitiously, we aim to produce profitable crops within an inclusive market system.&#xa0;Before this work takes place, a needs assessment will be carried out with the local communities to identify priorities and context specific adaptations.
Objective Two: Develop local, national and international campaigns on the importance of the Colombian Amazon
The Colombian Amazon, which covers around 10% of Colombia&#x2019;s land mass, experienced more than 2.3-million-hectare tree loss between 2002 and 2020. In spite of recent agreements reached at COP27 to curtail deforestation, action isn&#x2019;t being taken fast enough to reverse the damage it&#x2019;s caused to the planet. We seek to highlight how important the Amazon is to all our futures, through campaigns in the region and globally. This builds on our work with the custodians of the Brazilian Amazon rainforest, with a specific focus on working with young people.</narrative>
  </description>
